&lt;p&gt;You will be based in your home office around the Washington, DC area and you will report to the Regional Director of Federal Sales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceed quarterly and annual sales quotas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Play leadership role in executing sales plan for Federal Civilian Government business that delivers projected results and incorporates go-to-market, partners and resellers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead virtual teams of aligned resources (Sales Engineers, Inside Sales, Customer Success, Marketing, Executives, etc..) in winning business across their territory&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accomplish a complex, solution-based sales process encompassing multiple groups within a strategic account.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use our strong market position as the only FedRamp approved Collaborative Work Management solution available to federal agencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop new business opportunities by analyzing and proactively targeting high value needs across multiple departments and business lines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can effectively articulate and demonstrate Smartsheet’s unique business, solution and functional value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively develop unsolicited proposals that align with customer programs and position Smartsheet as an enterprise software solution provider&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively forecast sales opportunities, while tracking and using critical metrics that predict sales success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use Smartsheet in the execution of daily sales activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
