&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For over 20 years, Smartsheet has empowered teams to manage work seamlessly and scale solutions smarter. Now, in our most ambitious chapter yet, we are uniting human teams with AI agents. By orchestrating the work agents do best, automating manual tasks and uncovering insights at scale, we create the space for people to focus on what truly matters: judgment, creativity, and big thinking. That is magic at work, and it’s what we show up for every day.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a People Business Partner to support the execution of our talent strategy for our Product &amp;amp; Tech organization, serving our engineering and product teams. This role will report to the Manager, People Partnerships for Product &amp;amp; Technology, to execute talent initiatives and support our engineering and product leaders. This is a People Business Partner role for a professional with experience supporting engineering teams, from workforce planning and onboarding through performance management, development, and retention.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You excel at supporting engineering-centric talent initiatives by partnering with People &amp;amp; Culture Centers of Excellence across compensation, talent acquisition, benefits, and other People functions. You understand the unique dynamics of engineering roles, career ladders, and technical talent markets, and you support execution of programs that drive engineering effectiveness and retention.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will partner with Product &amp;amp; Tech leadership to support workforce planning and organizational needs, collaborate with People &amp;amp; Culture COEs to ensure consistent program delivery, and help execute People&amp;nbsp; solutions that support engineering excellence, team productivity, and business growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report to the Manager, People Business Partner. This is a hybrid role requiring three days per week in our Bellevue, WA office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product &amp;amp; Tech leadership to support workforce planning and organizational needs, ensuring alignment to business objectives and priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development and implementation of engineering-aligned talent management frameworks including performance management, retention strategies, and development programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach engineering managers on career development and management best practices; collaborate with the Employee Relations team to support performance feedback and employee relations matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional COEs to design and implement engineering-aligned talent systems and programs that remain competitive and support retention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support organizational design and workforce planning initiatives that improve team effectiveness, clarify roles, and support engineering productivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as strategic advisor to Product &amp;amp; Tech leadership on organizational effectiveness, talent optimization, compensation alignment, and talent initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor organizational health metrics specific to engineering teams, identify trends and opportunities, and support leadership in translating insights into action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support People &amp;amp; Culture initiatives and special projects as business needs evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5+ years of progressive People &amp;amp; Culture Business Partnership experience, with preference for experience supporting engineering or technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting engineering functions, with understanding of engineering organization dynamics, technical talent acquisition, engineer career progression, and engineering-specific retention challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record in a SaaS or software company environment preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working with employee data and organizational metrics; ability to identify trends and support leadership in data-informed decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and relationship-building skills with the ability to partner effectively with technical leaders and diverse team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, Psychology or related field; or equivalent years of relatable Human Resources experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Current US Perks &amp;amp; Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer subsidized medical/vision and dental coverage for full-time employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401k Match to help you save for your future (50% of your contribution up to the first 6% of your eligible pay)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly stipend to support your work and productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Time Away Program, plus Sick Time Off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US employees are automatically covered under Smartsheet-sponsored life insurance, short-term, and long-term disability plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US employees receive 12 paid holidays per year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Up to 24 weeks of Parental Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personal paid Volunteer Day to support our community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities for professional growth and development including access to Udemy online courses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company Funded Perks, including a counseling membership, local retail discounts, and your own personal Smartsheet account&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Teleworking options from any registered location in the U.S. (role specific)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
