&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For over 20 years, Smartsheet has empowered teams to manage work seamlessly and scale solutions smarter. Now, in our most ambitious chapter yet, we are uniting human teams with AI agents. By orchestrating the work agents do best, automating manual tasks and uncovering insights at scale, we create the space for people to focus on what truly matters: judgment, creativity, and big thinking. That is magic at work, and it’s what we show up for every day.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Smartsheet is looking for a regional &lt;strong&gt;Principal Channel Account Manager&lt;/strong&gt; for EMEA based in London. The primary focus will be to optimize, activate and recruit our &lt;strong&gt;French, Middle Eastern &amp;amp; Southern European channels&lt;/strong&gt; by managing and recruiting new solution partners. The channel account manager is a quota-carrying, revenue-producing role that is responsible for recruiting, onboarding and managing relationships with a defined portfolio of partners. The role is responsible for selective new partner recruitment against our ideal partner profile, engaging partners with the Smartsheet Aligned partner program, and driving joint partner business planning. Channel Account Managers will also significantly collaborate with Smartsheet direct sales teams locally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based at Smartsheet in &lt;strong&gt;London, UK (hybrid working cadence)&lt;/strong&gt; and reports to our &lt;strong&gt;Sr, Director - Partner Sales.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the multi-quarter and annual planning process with key partners, spanning enablement, co-marketing, sales pipeline, channel pipeline and forecast reporting; host QBRs and direct the actions that follow from them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive monthly partner alignment sessions, review pipelines, conduct win/loss analysis and direct account penetration strategy to build new sales opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the development of Smartsheet&#39;s EMEA partner strategy, defining which partner types, markets and segments the region pursues next, rather than recruiting against an existing profile&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the acknowledged authority on partner types across the region, including Service Partners, VARs, Referral Partners, Distributors, System Integrators and ISVs, and shape how that mix evolves as the region matures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the build out of a new partner segment or route to market for EMEA, taking it from concept through to a repeatable, revenue-generating motion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and grow partnerships in France, MEA and Southern Europe with accountability for how the model scales into new markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceed revenue targets by developing and maintaining relationships with potential and existing channel partners, and evangelise Collaborative Work Management as an emerging category to new partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the enablement and co-marketing agenda that direct sales, sales engineers and channel marketing follow, rather than coordinating with them as equal stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide input into partner strategy that other CAMs and regions adopt, establishing formal cross-functional networks that coordinate partner activity across the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide sales coaching and enablement, and hold partner organisations accountable for completing required training and certifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct the partner marketing plan with partners and the partner marketing manager, setting the strategy that drives demand against revenue targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the procurement relationship with our distributor, QBS in all relevant territories, including sign off on partner pricing, terms and deal structure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform other duties as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8 to 10 years of sales experience in Enterprise Application software. SaaS experience preferred. Understanding of a services led partner model, where the core value proposition for partners is delivering their own professional services. Not license transactions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability with partner recruitment and joint business planning.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to drive cross-functional teaming&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently resides in the greater London area. Willingness to commute into central London with some regularity, but not daily.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English is required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in French is desirable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Legally eligible to work in the UK on an ongoing basis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Perks &amp;amp; Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer-paid Private Medical and Dental, additional cost for family members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly contributions toward your pension&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly stipend to support your work and productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days paid for Holiday + Bank Holidays + Flexible Time Away Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;20 weeks fully paid Maternity Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12 weeks fully paid Paternity/Adoption Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personal paid Volunteer Day to support our community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities for professional growth and development including access to Udemy online courses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company Funded Perks including a counseling membership, salary sacrifice options, and your own personal Smartsheet account.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Teleworking options from any registered location in the UK (role specific)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
